      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Playground: train a classifier, paint its decision regions\n\nThe classic 2-D machine-learning picture, computed entirely in-graph (no inputs, no downloads): three Gaussian point clouds ('CV Random Points', 60 points each, deterministic seeds) become a labeled training set via 'CV Stack Feature Classes'. 'CV Train Classifier' splits it 75/25 per class, fits the model on the train split and reports held-out accuracy + a confusion matrix - the model lives and dies inside that one node, so you wire DATA through the graph, never a model handle.\n\nThe REGIONS: an 'CV Coordinate Grid' feeds every (x, y) of a 224x224 canvas (step 2) into query_features, so the trained model classifies the whole plane. 'CV Reshape Array' folds the flat predictions back to the grid (rows/cols wired straight from the grid node), cv2.convertScaleAbs spreads labels 0/1/2 to 0/100/200, cv2.resize (INTER_NEAREST - labels must not blend) blows it up, cv2.applyColorMap colors it and 'CV Draw Points' overlays the training points colored by class. Three classifiers run side by side on the SAME data: the SVM (RBF) bends smoothly around the clouds, KNearest follows individual points (wiggly islands), RTrees paints axis-aligned rectangles - compare the three region previews.\n\nFAILURE PATH (bottom): two empty point sets (count = 0) stack into a zero-sample training set. The trainer reports success=false with safe outputs (query predictions all fall back to one class) instead of raising - detection/estimation failures are data, not errors."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
